{"timestamp": 1779401537.975809, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I found Eve\u2019s body in Navigation and reported immediately. My route was Medbay -> Upper Engine -> Lower Engine -> Storage -> Navigation. I didn\u2019t encounter anyone at all on the way, so I can\u2019t vouch for anyone or say who was near Nav. Bob is also dead, apparently in Weapons, but I never went there. Need locations from everyone, especially anyone near Navigation or Weapons."}}
{"timestamp": 1779401554.3304691, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I was up top for most of the round. My route was Oxygen, then through Cafeteria, and I was finishing up in Electrical when the meeting was called. I didn't cross paths with Eve or Bob at all, so I don't have any info on their locations. \n\nCharlie, since you didn't see anyone leaving Navigation through Storage, the killer must have gone up towards Security. Alice, Diana, where were you two? If you were on the right side of the map, you must have seen someone or something."}}
{"timestamp": 1779401578.989844, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "My route was Security -> Weapons -> Cafeteria -> Oxygen -> Upper Engine -> Lower Engine, and I ended in Lower Engine. I didn\u2019t see anyone at all, and I also did not see Bob\u2019s body when I passed through Weapons, so if Bob really died there, I think it happened after I left Weapons.\n\nThat makes me want to hear Diana\u2019s exact path. Frank says he was Oxygen -> Cafeteria -> Electrical, but I went through Cafeteria/Oxygen too and didn\u2019t see him, so timing matters there. Charlie reporting Eve in Navigation makes sense if killer left toward Security, but Bob in Weapons points to someone being on the top/right side too. I don\u2019t have a hard accusation yet, but Diana needs to give a very clear route."}}
{"timestamp": 1779401604.195615, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "My route was Electrical -> Security -> Weapons -> Cafeteria -> Medbay -> Upper Engine, where I ended. I saw Eve in Security around ticks 6 and 7, and then I saw her leave Security toward Navigation at tick 8. I did not see her again after that.\n\nI also passed through Weapons after Security and I did not see Bob\u2019s body there, so I agree Bob likely died later than my pass-through too.\n\nThe big thing for me is Eve: she was alive going from Security into Navigation, and Charlie later finds her body in Navigation. That means whoever killed Eve either came from Storage side or Security side after tick 8. Charlie could be a self-report, but his route to Nav through Storage fits finding it. Frank ending Electrical after being Oxygen/Cafeteria also puts him near the right side path, and Alice\u2019s Security -> Weapons start overlaps the area but maybe timing was earlier.\n\nI\u2019m most suspicious of Frank or possibly Charlie here. Frank\u2019s story doesn\u2019t line up great with Alice not seeing him around Caf/Oxygen, and he had access toward Electrical/Security/Nav side. I don\u2019t think I can clear Charlie, but Frank feels like the better vote to me unless someone has stronger timing."}}
{"timestamp": 1779401625.52543, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "To add to my report: I entered Navigation from Storage and found Eve\u2019s body there immediately. I saw nobody in Storage, the Storage-Nav corridor, or Navigation besides the body.\n\nMy full route was Medbay -> Upper Engine -> Lower Engine -> Storage -> Navigation, and I didn\u2019t see any living players the whole round. So I can\u2019t clear anyone.\n\nDiana\u2019s claim that Eve left Security toward Navigation is important. If true, the killer either followed from Security/Nav side or came in from Storage before I arrived. I didn\u2019t see anyone leaving toward Storage, so Security side feels more likely. Between the stories, Frank being on Oxygen/Cafeteria/Electrical and not being seen by Alice is a little odd, but I\u2019m not 100% sure. I\u2019m leaning Frank right now unless someone has better timing."}}
{"timestamp": 1779401651.994147, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Hold on, there is a massive glaring contradiction between Alice and Diana's stories. \n\nAlice, you said you started in Security, went to Weapons, then Cafeteria, and you saw ABSOLUTELY NO ONE. \nDiana, you claim you went Electrical -> Security -> Weapons -> Cafeteria, AND you saw Eve in Security at ticks 6 and 7. \n\nHow is it possible that both of you took almost the exact same path from Security to Cafeteria, yet Alice didn't see you OR Eve? If Diana was trailing right behind you or crossing through the same rooms, one of you should have seen the other, and Alice definitely should have seen Eve. \n\nAlice, regarding us not seeing each other: I was in Oxygen for a while doing tasks, then went down through Cafeteria to Electrical. We likely just passed each other while one of us was in a corridor or transitioning. But Diana claiming to be in the exact same sequence of rooms as you and seeing people you didn't? That's a huge red flag.\n\nDiana is pushing me hard to distract from this huge hole in her story. I think Diana caught Eve on the right side, killed her, and then got Bob later, and she's trying to fabricate a route that overlaps with Alice to sound safe. I'm voting Diana, this contradiction is too big to ignore."}}
{"timestamp": 1779401676.33569, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "Frank, I don\u2019t think the Alice/Diana thing is as \u201cmassive\u201d a contradiction as you\u2019re making it sound. I started in Security and moved on; Diana says she came Electrical -> Security and saw Eve there at ticks 6-7. If I had already left Security/Weapons before that, it\u2019s completely possible I wouldn\u2019t see either of them.\n\nWhat stands out more to me is Bob in Weapons. I passed Weapons and saw no body. Diana says she also passed Weapons and saw no body. Charlie never went there. Frank, you were the one claiming to be up top around Oxygen/Cafeteria, which is closest to Weapons, and neither I nor anyone else saw you.\n\nFor Eve, Diana\u2019s info puts Eve alive leaving Security toward Navigation. Charlie finds her from Storage side and sees nobody. That could be Security-side access, which Frank had from Electrical/Security area. Diana is possible, but Frank\u2019s route fits both Bob in Weapons and access toward Eve\u2019s side better to me.\n\nI\u2019m leaning Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779401695.362248, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Frank is exaggerating the timing issue to make it sound like a contradiction when it isn\u2019t one. Alice started in Security and moved on; I came from Electrical into Security later and saw Eve there at ticks 6 and 7, then watched Eve leave toward Navigation at tick 8. That fully explains why Alice didn\u2019t see Eve or me.\n\nMy route stayed consistent: Electrical -> Security -> Weapons -> Cafeteria -> Medbay -> Upper Engine. I passed Weapons after Security and saw no Bob body, same as Alice. So Bob died after both of us had already gone through Weapons.\n\nFrank is the only one whose route fits both deaths well: he claims Oxygen -> Cafeteria -> Electrical, putting him near Weapons for Bob and then near Electrical/Security/Navigation side for Eve. Also nobody saw him, and Alice specifically says she was in the same general upper area and didn\u2019t cross him.\n\nCharlie self-report is possible, but Frank feels much more likely based on opportunity and how hard he\u2019s trying to force suspicion onto me with a timing argument that doesn\u2019t actually hold. I\u2019m voting Frank."}}
